What is Stack?

Definition:

A Stack is a Linear Data Structure that follows the LIFO principle.

LIFO = Last In First Out

Why do we use Stack?

Stack is used whenever we need to remember the latest data first.

Examples:

Undo operation (Ctrl + Z)
Browser Back Button
Function Calls
Expression Evaluation
Parentheses Matching
DFS (Depth First Search)
Recursion

Stack Operations

There are only 5 important operations.

=>push()

=>pop()

=>peek()

=>isEmpty()

=>size()
Push=>Push means Insert an element.
Pop=>Pop means Remove Top element.
Peek=>Peek means See Top element.Don't remove.
isEmpty()=>Checks whether stack is empty.

